{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Defs"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.mu4_unconstrained_below_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.mu4_unconstrained_below_four","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellSlotAlignment.lean#L186-L194","doc":"**No 3-particle measurement determines `μ₄`.** Two simplex ansätze differing\n*only* in their 4-body moment agree on `M(A)` for every `A ≤ 3`, because the\n`C(A,4)` column vanishes there. Hence nothing measured on a 3-particle cluster —\nat any bond order, `Δ²g`, `Δ³g`, or higher — constrains `μ₄`; a genuine `μ₄`\ncomparand requires `A = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.mu4_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.mu4_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellSlotAlignment.lean#L180-L184","doc":"The recursive form agrees with the closed alternating (finite-difference)\nform `μ₄ = M₄ − 4M₃ + 6M₂`. Recorded because the compute uses the recursion and\nthe exposition quotes the closed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.mu_inversion_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.mu_inversion_four","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellSlotAlignment.lean#L173-L178","doc":"**Binomial inversion at `A = 4`.** The 4-body moment is\n`μ₄ = M₄ − 6μ₂ − 4μ₃`, matching the compute's recursive form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.mu_inversion_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.mu_inversion_three","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellSlotAlignment.lean#L167-L171","doc":"**Binomial inversion at `A = 3`.** From the ansatz, the 3-body moment is\n`μ₃ = M₃ − 3μ₂` — the recursion used by the residual-simplex compute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.Mval_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.Mval_four","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellSlotAlignment.lean#L163-L165","doc":"`M(4) = 6μ₂ + 4μ₃ + μ₄`: `C(4,2) = 6`, `C(4,3) = 4`, `C(4,4) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.Mval_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.Mval_three","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellSlotAlignment.lean#L159-L161","doc":"`M(3) = 3μ₂ + μ₃`: `C(3,2) = 3`, `C(3,3) = 1`, `C(3,4) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.Mval_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.Mval_two","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellSlotAlignment.lean#L155-L157","doc":"`M(2) = μ₂`: only the edge column is populated at `A = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.Mval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.Mval","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellSlotAlignment.lean#L149-L153","doc":"The residual-simplex ansatz `M(A) = ∑_k μ_k · C(A,k)`, with the binomial\ncoefficients taken from `Nat.choose` rather than hand-substituted, so that the\ncombinatorics is part of the statement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.triple_must_dominate_of_moment_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.triple_must_dominate_of_moment_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellSlotAlignment.lean#L132-L141","doc":"The contrapositive, as the programme uses it: to get a **non-positive**\nassembled moment, the triple must be at least as large in magnitude as the whole\npair total. A triple that is merely negative does not suffice — which is exactly\nwhy the measured `Δ³g < 0` does not open the sign door. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.moment_pos_of_triple_dominated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.moment_pos_of_triple_dominated","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellSlotAlignment.lean#L115-L130","doc":"**The measured configuration: the sign obstruction survives the slot\ncorrection.** If the triple difference exceeds minus the total of the three pair\ndifferences, the assembled 3-body moment is strictly positive. With the three\npair differences measured positive (total `≈ 1.23`) and the triple measured\n`≈ -0.33`, the hypothesis holds comfortably, so the assembled moment carries the\npair differences' sign — correcting the slot from `Δ²g` to `∑Δ²g + Δ³g` cannot\nflip the sign verdict.\n\nThe decomposition is load-bearing here: the conclusion is about `bodyMoment3`,\nwhich is only connected to the hypothesis through `triangle_moment_decomp`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.moment_eq_pair_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.moment_eq_pair_iff","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellSlotAlignment.lean#L99-L107","doc":"Likewise, the single pair difference is the moment only when the other two\npairs and the triple cancel against it — so `Δ²g(a,b)` alone is not the\ncomparand either. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.moment_eq_triple_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.moment_eq_triple_iff","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellSlotAlignment.lean#L89-L97","doc":"**When reading `Δ³g` as the moment is legitimate.** The triple difference\nequals the 3-body moment exactly when the three pair differences cancel. Since\nthey are measured strictly positive (and hence do not cancel), the shortcut is\ninvalid for this operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.triangle_moment_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.triangle_moment_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellSlotAlignment.lean#L78-L87","doc":"**The slot-alignment identity.** The 3-body moment of the triangle is the sum\nof the three pair differences **plus** the triple difference — neither piece\nalone. This is the statement that fixes which measured quantity is the `μ₃`\ncomparand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.bodyMoment3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.bodyMoment3","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellSlotAlignment.lean#L73-L76","doc":"The 3-body moment of a triangle: total interaction minus the sum of the\nsingle-bond (2-body) pieces, `μ₃ = M₃ − 3μ₂` with `M₃ = g_{abc} − g_∅` and\n`μ₂ = g_x − g_∅`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.tripleDiff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.tripleDiff","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellSlotAlignment.lean#L69-L71","doc":"The triple (Ursell) mixed difference over three bonds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.pairDiff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment.pairDiff","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellSlotAlignment.lean#L66-L67","doc":"The second mixed difference over two bonds: `Δ²g(x,y) = g_{xy} − g_x − g_y + g_∅`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}